🧠 Deadlock Memory Sheet (Save This)
Deadlock

Definition:
Two or more threads wait forever for each other's locks.

Requirements:
✅ Two or more threads
✅ Two or more locks
✅ Circular waiting

Cause:
Different lock acquisition order

Prevention:
Always acquire locks in the same order
Interview Questions You Can Now Answer

If an interviewer asks:

❓What is Deadlock?

A deadlock is a situation where two or more threads wait indefinitely for each other 
to release resources, preventing all of them from continuing execution.

❓What causes Deadlock?

Multiple threads acquiring multiple locks in different orders, resulting in circular 
waiting.

❓How do you prevent Deadlock?

Acquire locks in the same order, minimize nested locking, and keep the duration of 
holding locks as short as possible.